{"id":"000VS8","title":"[TSL][S2T2] The Detoured Route","author":"Donatello_86","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":5,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-30T05:57:07+00:00","posted":"Heute, 06:11 Uhr","rules":"[TSL][S2T2]The Detoured Route\n\nThis puzzle was made for the skunkworks league held by Damasosos92. The idea was to have two distinct puzzles interacting with each other. The judges felt my submission would be better combined. This is the result. This is my most difficult puzzle to date, which was not intended. Feel free to leave any type of comment\n\nRules:\n\n-Place the digits one through nine once each in every row, column, and 3X3 box.\n\nNUMBERED ROOMS:\n\n-A digit equal to the clue outside the grid is placed in the Nth cell from the clue in its respective row or column, where N is the digit placed closest to the clue.\n\nENTROPIC LINES:\n\n-Any set of three sequential cells along a peach entropic line must contain a digit from each of the three sets {1,2,3}, {4,5,6} and {7,8,9}.\n\nPATH:\n\n-Draw a path that moves orthogonally throughout the grid and outside perimeter. The path never moves diagonally.\n\n-The path enters through the green line above column 1 and exits through the green line below column 8. Part of the path is given.\n\n-The path may intersect but may not branch or overlap.\n\n-In regards, to cells belonging to either the Nth cell of a NUMBERED ROOMS clue or a digit on an ENTROPIC LINE:\n\nA. Low digits {1,2,3}, places a straight-line segment inside the cell.\n\nB. Middle digits {4,5,6}, places a turn inside the cell.\n\nC. High digits {7,8,9}, places an intersection inside the cell.\n\nCIRCLES:-All circles are on the path.\n\n-A digit placed inside a circle counts the number of path segments which the circle is part of between one or two intersections or between an entrance/exit and intersection. The intersection is not part of the count.\n\n-A digit in a circle that is placed on the outside perimeter of the grid acts in duality as a Numbered Rooms clue and a count of path segments. A cell outside the grid without a given clue or circle, is NOT a numbered rooms clue\n\nCircles Examples:\n\nSudokupad\n\nPuzzle:","solutionCode":"The digits between the intersections which the R5C4 circle is part of in reading order","tags":["Sudoku","Entropie (Thema)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/o2znumpb7m","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/o2znumpb7m","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":11,"cols":11,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-30T05:57:07+00:00"}